# Radar Chart — Skia radar chart (5 axes, 5 grid layers, two filled polygons with
# dots) whose values spring to new random data on SHUFFLE; a shuffle during a
# running spring re-bases from the interpolated values (cancelAnimation path).
# What this test covers: single shuffles with the spring allowed to settle,
# bursts of rapid shuffles that interrupt the spring mid-flight (the
# progress < 1 re-interpolation branch), a press-and-hold on the button, and a
# final settle.
context platform=ios
open "demos://animations/radar-chart"
wait "label=\"Close\"" 45000
# Warm-up touch on the status bar: the first touch of a test can be lost while
# the XCTest runner attaches.
press 330 20
wait 500
wait "text" "SHUFFLE" 10000
wait 1000
press "label=\"SHUFFLE\""
wait 1500
press "label=\"SHUFFLE\""
wait 1500
# Burst: five shuffles 120ms apart, each interrupting the previous spring.
press 200 663 --count 5 --interval-ms 120
wait 300
press 200 663 --count 3 --interval-ms 60
wait 2000
# Long hold on the button (PressableScale scale-down, release fires onPress).
longpress 200 663 900
wait 1500
press "label=\"SHUFFLE\""
wait 250
press "label=\"SHUFFLE\""
wait 2000
wait "text" "SHUFFLE" 3000
wait "label=\"Close\"" 15000
press "role=\"button\" label=\"Close\""
wait 1500
